  "id": "10278",
  "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10278",
  "key": "AIN-49",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[Data model] Enforce tenant-safe references, uniqueness and valid state constraints",
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Parent owns shared data-model implementation. Planning priority: foundational. Preserve existing behavior through additive changes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Current state"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Application-level checks coexist with database constraints; commercial ledgers already have useful immutable triggers and compound references. Fee uses polymorphic chargedToEntityType/Id, and several lifecycle states are strings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Deliverables and acceptance criteria"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletList",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Inventory existing constraints before adding any; define an explicit integrity matrix for same-tenant references, version references, external IDs, idempotency keys and allowed states."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Add appropriate foreign keys, composite unique/check constraints and transaction-safe transition enforcement; document service-boundary references where a database FK is impossible."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Prove invalid direct writes and concurrent duplicate writes are rejected, while valid legacy fixtures migrate without deletion."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Related domain work"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "AIN-21, AIN-34, AIN-43. Coordinate contracts with these tickets; do not reimplement their business workflows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Single-developer sprint sequence \u2014 2026-11-04"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Target candidate: AIN S03 | Database integrity and CI (Jira sprint 38)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sprint outcome: Enforce the reviewed tenant/reference/state constraints and make drift detectable in CI."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Exit evidence: Valid legacy fixtures migrate; direct invalid writes and concurrent duplicates fail; model/migration drift checks pass."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Planning envelope: 6 implementation days + 2 integrated verification days + 1 review/refinement day + 1 contingency day; not measured velocity. One primary outcome in progress; at most two closely related workflow slices. Story/task pairs share effort, not double-counted work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Existing active sprint remains active with original dates; only its goal/name and unfinished membership are reorganized. Every new sprint is future and undated. No fabricated story-point/time estimates or assignees. The ordered slots are a provisional work breakdown, not a fixed delivery forecast. Before activation, split any candidate exceeding six implementation days and verify reviewer/provider readiness; preserve all parent acceptance criteria."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Scheduling is not implementation: original AC/DoD and parent scope are unchanged. Related story/task/subtask effort is one delivery slice, not additive capacity. Required domain slices can be delivered earlier than the broader owner completion sprint; no broader item is Done until all original requirements pass."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
